#!/usr/sbin/nft -f
# demo-int isolation (invariant I4). Insert the three-way policy at the TOP of
# Docker's DOCKER-USER chain (dockerd creates DOCKER-USER; do NOT redefine it as
# a base chain). `insert` prepends, so these are listed bottom-up to land in the
# right order: established/related first, then warden->instance ALLOW, then the
# two DENYs. Subnet-matched (172.31.0.0/24) so the bridge name is irrelevant;
# warden static addr = 172.31.0.2. Instances run cap_drop:[ALL] (no CAP_NET_RAW),
# so they cannot source-spoof 172.31.0.2.
#
#   warden  -> instance : ALLOW (the proxy path)
#   instance-> warden   : DENY  (can't reach the control plane / socket-proxy)
#   instance-> instance : DENY  (can't reach a peer)
#
# ⚠️ Gate-1/Gate-3: run AFTER docker.service (a systemd oneshot), confirm ordering
# survives a daemon reload, and make re-application idempotent (flush the demo
# rules by handle before re-inserting) so repeated runs don't stack duplicates.
insert rule ip filter DOCKER-USER ip saddr 172.31.0.0/24 ip daddr 172.31.0.0/24 drop
insert rule ip filter DOCKER-USER ip daddr 172.31.0.2 ip saddr 172.31.0.0/24 drop
insert rule ip filter DOCKER-USER ip saddr 172.31.0.2 tcp dport 8000 accept
insert rule ip filter DOCKER-USER ct state established,related accept
